SimPhy-X is a modified version of SimPhy 1.0.2:

  SimPhy: A comprehensive simulator of gene family evolution
  Copyright (C) 2015 Diego Mallo, Leonardo de Oliveira Martins and David Posada
  https://github.com/adamallo/SimPhy (tag v1.0.2, commit b36f07a)

The SimPhy paper (Mallo, de Oliveira Martins and Posada, Systematic Biology
65(2):334-344, 2016, doi:10.1093/sysbio/syv082) states that "SimPhy is
distributed under the license GNU GPL v3". SimPhy-X is distributed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 (SPDX: GPL-3.0-only); the license text is
in LICENSE.

Changes relative to SimPhy 1.0.2 (2026):
  * The simulator was re-implemented in C (src/) following SimPhy 1.0.2's source
    and random-number consumption order, with array-based trees, linear memory
    and a thread pool.
  * New default "compat" mode: output byte-identical to SimPhy 1.0.2 for the
    same command line and seed, at any thread count.
  * New "fast" mode (-XM fast): independent random streams per locus and
    uniformisation-based sampling of the bounded coalescent instead of 512-bit
    MPFR root finding.
  * New options -XM, -XT, -XR and -XV; a SimPhy-X banner before SimPhy's
    program text; the help text lists the new options.
  * Inputs on which SimPhy 1.0.2 crashes or reads uninitialised memory are
    handled deterministically (DOCS/03-usage.md, "Fixed trees as input").

The SimPhy 1.0.2 source itself is referenced as a git submodule in
upstream/SimPhy and is used, unmodified, only to build the reference binary for
the byte-exact tests.

